REVERSE-ENGINEERED GRAPH ARCHITECTURE
Node Model (brain_objects + Subtype Tables): Polymorphic Class-Table Inheritance. Every node registers an immutable (id UUID, object_type) row in brain_objects via new_object(type), then stores specialized attributes in sources, wiki_pages, entities, concepts, artifacts, decisions, projects, studios, or agents. Hydrated for the UI into BrainNode (id, title, category, kind, area, summary, notes, stalenessDays, needsAttention, connections[], tags[], x, y, z, radius, targetPositions).
Edge Model (relationships): Directed, typed, provenance-backed edges (from_id, to_id, edge_type, confidence, source_id, review_state, superseded_at, metadata) with a self-loop check (from_id <> to_id) and non-destructive soft-deprecation (superseded_at, review_state = 'rejected').
Graph Storage & Traversal: PostgreSQL relational adjacency table indexed on (from_id, to_id) and (to_id, from_id). Multi-hop traversal executes inside PostgreSQL via the cycle-safe recursive CTE function graph_neighbors(start_id, max_depth) using an array visited UUID[] path check (NOT (r.to_id = ANY(g.visited))) over active non-rejected edges.
Graph Rendering Engine (Brain3D.tsx): Custom Three.js WebGLRenderer (with software WebGL/SwiftShader frame throttling and hardware MSAA detection) rendering:
Distinct geometries per NodeKind (BoxGeometry, OctahedronGeometry, TorusGeometry, CylinderGeometry, SphereGeometry) with emissive glow rings for key anchors and attention alerts.
A single batched THREE.LineSegments buffer for all active edges (recolored dynamically on hover/selection/focus isolation).
Smooth vector interpolation (lerp) when morphing between 6 layouts (orbit, rings, circle, areas, links, timeline).
3D-to-2D viewport projection (Vector3.project(camera)) updating DOM <button> labels directly via style.transform = translate3d(...) outside React render cycles for 60fps fluidity.
Real-Time & Optimistic Updates: Client-side additions merge optimistically (customNodes), while persistent ingestions enqueue an idempotent source_created / artifact_created record inside PostgreSQL events and claim/process asynchronously via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED (claim_events()).
Persistence Layer: Zero-config persistence: remote DATABASE_URL uses postgres + native vector(1536) HNSW; local mode spins up embedded @electric-sql/pglite on disk with a custom vector domain (real[]) and PL/pgSQL <=> cosine distance operator so identical SQL runs in both environments.
Search & Filtering: Client-side real-time filtering by searchQuery (title/tags), category, area, kind, needsAttention, and 1–2 hop focusIsolation; Server-side Hybrid Search (GET /api/search) runs parallel Postgres English FTS (ts_rank_cd) and vector similarity (1 - (embedding <=> query_vec)) combined via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (1/(60+rank)) and enriched with verbatim claims citations.
Knowledge Linking Engine (librarian-pipeline.ts): Converts raw notes/sources into structured entities, concepts, cross-edges, wiki pages, verbatim line-located claims (line X), and 900-char overlapping embedding chunks, deduplicating similar nodes via pg_trgm similarity > 0.82 and non-destructive merged_into_id pointers.
