MIGRATION GUIDE
1. Installation
Copy packages/graph-engine into your target monorepo/repository and install peer and runtime dependencies:
Bash
npm install three @types/three lucide-react @google/genai postgres @electric-sql/pglite
If using Next.js App Router, add @cortex/graph-engine to transpilePackages in next.config.ts (or map @/packages/graph-engine in tsconfig.json).
2. Environment Variables
Add to .env.local:
Env
# Omit DATABASE_URL to run zero-config persistent local PostgreSQL via PGlite
DATABASE_URL=
GRAPH_PGDATA_DIR=.graph-engine/pgdata

# Optional: enables gemini-embedding-001 (1536 dims), entity extraction, and node Q&A
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: custom API key if wiring GraphAuthGuard
GRAPH_API_KEY=
3. Database Setup
Local PGlite (Zero-Config): Calling any server function (createGraphApiHandlers) automatically creates .graph-engine/pgdata, registers the vector (real[]) domain and <=> cosine distance operator shim, and runs schema.sql.
Production PostgreSQL 15+: Ensure pgvector, pg_trgm, and pgcrypto extensions are available; ensureGraphSchemaMigrated() automatically provisions vector(1536) + the HNSW cosine index.
4. Next.js API Routes Setup
Create thin route handlers delegating directly to createGraphApiHandlers:
